Step 1 — Create VPC

        Go to:

            AWS Console → VPC → Create VPC

        Configuration

        Field                   Value

        Name                    demo-vpc
        IPv4 CIDR               10.0.0.0/16

=================================================================

Step 2 — Create Public Subnet

        VPC → Subnets → Create subnet

        Field           Value

        Name            public-subnet
        CIDR            10.0.1.0/24
        AZ              ap-south-2a

        Enable:

            Auto-assign public IPv4

            This is IMPORTANT.


===============================================================

Step 3 — Create Private Subnet

        Field   Value

        Name    private-subnet
        CIDR    10.0.2.0/24
        AZ      ap-south-1a

        Do NOT enable public IP.

--------------------------------------------------------------

Step 4 — Create Internet Gateway (IGW)

        VPC → Internet Gateways → Create

       Field   Value
        Name    demo-igw

        After creation:

                Actions → Attach to VPC

        Attach to:

                demo-vpc

--------------------------------------------------------------

Step 5 — Create Public Route Table

        VPC → Route Tables → Create

  Field   Value
   Name    public-rt

     Add Route:

        Destination: 0.0.0.0/0
        
        Target: Internet Gateway (demo-igw)

     Associate:

        public-subnet

------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 6 — Create Elastic IP

        VPC → Elastic IPs → Allocate

        This is needed for NAT Gateway.

---------------------------------------------------------------

Step 7 — Create NAT Gateway

        VPC → NAT Gateways → Create

  Field            Value
   Name           demo-nat
   Subnet         public-subnet  IMP *****************
   Elastic IP     select allocated EIP

Why public subnet?

        Because NAT needs internet access.


------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 8 — Create Private Route Table

        VPC → Route Tables → Create

  Field   Value
   Name    private-rt

Add Route:

  Destination: 0.0.0.0/0
  Target: NAT Gateway

Associate:

   private-subnet

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 9 — Create NACL

        VPC → Network ACLs → Create

  Field   Value
   Name    demo-nacl

Associate with:

    public-subnet
    private-subnet

----------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 10 — Configure NACL Rules

        Inbound Rules

        Rule    Type            Port    Source  Allow/Deny
        100     HTTP            80      0.0.0.0/0       ALLOW
        110     HTTPS           443     0.0.0.0/0       ALLOW
        120     SSH             22      YOUR-IP/32      ALLOW
        130     Custom TCP  1024-65535  0.0.0.0/0       Allow



        Outbound Rules

        Rule    Type            Port            Destination             Allow/Deny
        100     ALL Traffic     ALL             0.0.0.0/0               ALLOW
        110     Custom TCP      1024-65535      0.0.0.0/100             ALLOW

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 11 — Create Web Server Security Group

        VPC → Security Groups → Create

Field   Value
   Name    web-sg

Inbound Rules

        Type    Port    Source
        HTTP    80      0.0.0.0/0
        HTTPS   443     0.0.0.0/0
        SSH     22      Your-IP

Outbound:

     Allow All

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 12 — Create App Server Security Group

        Field   Value
         Name    app-sg


        Inbound Rules

        Type                    Port    Source
        Custom TCP              8000    web-sg
        SSH                     22      web-sg

Meaning:

        ONLY web server can talk to app server.

        No public internet access.

Outbound:

        Allow All

